# Project structure

Follow `.cursor/skills/project-structure/SKILL.md` when adding pages, placing components, or choosing SSR vs CSR exports.

Hard rules:

- kebab-case **files and folders**; PascalCase **component exports**
- Document shell in `app/layout.tsx`; locale + `NextIntlClientProvider` in `app/[locale]/layout.tsx`
- Default public UI in `(site)/`; optional groups: `(entry)` auth, `(console)` app, `(landing)` campaigns
- Entry/console chrome in `src/layouts/`; the group `layout.tsx` composes it. `(site)` chrome stays in `(site)/layout.tsx`
- Shared list/detail chrome in `src/components/feature-shell/`
- Design-system primitives in `src/components/ui/` when a UI recipe is applied; import via `@/components/ui`
- APIs, constants, and utils in `src/lib/`; group view models in `<group>/_handlers/`; rare shared hooks in `src/hooks/`; bootstrap in `src/configs/`
- Route-group UI in `<group>/_components/`; multi-page dual SSR/CSR UI in `[locale]/_shared/`
- `server.tsx` / `client.tsx` are export entries only — never import both from a sibling file
- `template.tsx` is the view; `skeleton.tsx` is loading; CSS modules use `<page>-<component>.module.css`
- Prefer `type` over `interface`; path alias `@/*` → `src/*`
